summary:
  A tick notes the player's position as the place heard without asking whether it can be one.

history:
  At the end of a Matroska buffer the player puts its position at the
  header's length while it still says it plays, and the end itself comes a
  moment later. Noted as the place heard, that length is where the reopen
  would go.

target:
  package/contents/ui/TimeshiftEngine.qml

find:
  TimeshiftLogic.endPlaceMs(pos, _captured(now), _heardPosMs)

replace:
  Number(pos)

expect:
  Killed by tst_timeshiftengine::test_the_headers_length_is_not_a_place_the_reader_was_seen_at.
  Line-neutral.
